    "field": "Past species distribution modeling",
    "problem": "Paleoecological studies are hindered by the spatial and temporal gaps in the fossil record, making the analysis of past biotas and their geographical distributions difficult or impossible, a challenge which Species Distribution Models (SDMs) can help overcome by complementing the available fossil information.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a methodology using Species Distribution Models (SDMs), calibrated with fossil records and paleoclimatic simulations, to model past species distributions, thus complementing the incomplete fossil record and enabling analyses of paleoecological questions like extinction dynamics.",
    "task": "The task is to review and demonstrate the application of Species Distribution Models to reconstruct the past geographic distribution and extinction dynamics of species for paleoecological studies, using *Smilodon populator* as a case study.",
